  "summary": "The ACLU of Northern California submitted an analysis of Alameda's draft ALPR policy ahead of a city council public forum, warning that the policy lacks safeguards on collection, use, retention, and access. The ACLU urges Alameda not to adopt ALPR technology until strong, enforceable safeguards are in place.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "As currently drafted, the Alameda policy manual raises significant privacy and civil liberties concerns because it lacks safeguards on the collection, use and retention of data collected from drivers in the city.",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "We urge Alameda not to adopt ALPR technology until a set of strong, enforceable safeguards is adopted following an open process of public input and debate.",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    }
